    "slug": "user-guide/guides",
    "title": "Guides",
    "description": "Step-by-step walkthroughs for the most common Checkstack operator tasks.",
    "headings": [],
    "content": "These guides walk through the most common things you do as an operator: configuring your first health check, connecting a satellite, wiring up notifications, setting up SSO, managing teams, opening and resolving incidents, scheduling maintenance, installing plugins, getting started with GitOps, and silencing alerts during a known disruption.\n\nIf you are looking for the mental model behind these workflows, read the [Concepts](/checkstack/user-guide/concepts/) section first.",
